## Generate a Bitrise Personal Access Token (PAT)

An API token is required to authenticate the MCP server against your personal Bitrise account permissions:

1. Log in to [Bitrise.io](https://app.bitrise.io).
2. In the top right corner, click on your **Profile Avatar** and select **Account settings**.
3. In the left navigation menu, click **Security**.
4. Scroll down to the **Personal Access Tokens** section and click **Generate new token**.
5. Enter a descriptive token name: `Bitrise MCP Gateway`.
6. Set the token expiration to **3 months** (90 days).
7. Ensure all workspace and application permissions remain checked so the MCP server can list apps, inspect artifacts, and trigger builds on your behalf.
8. Click **Generate**.
9. **Copy the generated PAT immediately and store it securely.** Bitrise will never display this token again once you close the modal.

