## Configure the MCP Server in TrueFoundry

### Navigate to the MCP Gateway
1. Log in to **TrueFoundry** using your enterprise SSO credentials.
2. In the left-hand navigation menu, select **MCP Gateway**.

### Select the Environment and Server
1. Select the target environment: **`dev`** (or **`prod`** for production release operations).
2. In the MCP Server Registry, locate **`bitrise-mcp-server`**.
3. Click on the card to open the server details view.

### Add an Auth Override with Your Bitrise PAT
1. In the server details panel, click the **Auth Overrides** tab.
2. Click **+ Add Auth Override**.
3. Paste the Bitrise Personal Access Token (PAT) generated earlier.
4. Click **Save Override**. The gateway now uses your credentials whenever your coding agent sends MCP tool calls.

